    </p><a href="/">← Home</a><pagefind-searchbox></pagefind-searchbox><script type="module" src="/pagefind/pagefind-component-ui.js"></script><script type="text/javascript" src="/static/pagefind.js"></script><h1 class="register-section" data-pagefind-body="1" data-pagefind-weight="10" data-pagefind-sort="title">TRCCNTVR&lt;n&gt;, n = 0 - 3</h1><p class="insn_subtitle" data-pagefind-body="1">Trace Counter Value Register &lt;n&gt;</p><div data-pagefind-body="1">
        <p>This sets or returns the value of Counter &lt;n&gt;.</p>
      </div><h3>Configuration</h3><p>External register TRCCNTVR&lt;n&gt; bits [31:0] are architecturally mapped to AArch64 System register <a href="AArch64-trccntvrn.html">TRCCNTVR&lt;n&gt;[31:0]</a>.</p><p>This register is present only when FEAT_ETE is implemented and FEAT_TRC_EXT is implemented. Otherwise, direct accesses to TRCCNTVR&lt;n&gt; are <span class="arm-defined-word">RES0</span>.</p><h3>Attributes</h3>
        <p>TRCCNTVR&lt;n&gt; is a 32-bit register.</p>
      <h2>Field descriptions</h2><table class="regdiagram" id="fieldset_0"><thead><tr><td>31</td><td>30</td><td>29</td><td>28</td><td>27</td><td>26</td><td>25</td><td>24</td><td>23</td><td>22</td><td>21</td><td>20</td><td>19</td><td>18</td><td>17</td><td>16</td><td>15</td><td>14</td><td>13</td><td>12</td><td>11</td><td>10</td><td>9</td><td>8</td><td>7</td><td>6</td><td>5</td><td>4</td><td>3</td><td>2</td><td>1</td><td>0</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr class="firstrow"><td class="lr" colspan="16"><a href="#fieldset_0-31_16">RES0</a></td><td class="lr" colspan="16"><a href="#fieldset_0-15_0">VALUE</a></td></tr></tbody></table><h4 id="fieldset_0-31_16">Bits [31:16]:
      </h4><div class="field">
      <p>Reserved, <span class="arm-defined-word">RES0</span>.</p>
    </div><h4 id="fieldset_0-15_0">VALUE, bits [15:0]:
      </h4><div class="field">
      <p>Contains the count value of Counter.</p>
    <p>The reset behavior of this field is:</p><ul><li>On a Trace unit reset, 
      this field resets
       to an architecturally <span class="arm-defined-word">UNKNOWN</span> value.</li></ul></div><h2>Accessing TRCCNTVR&lt;n&gt;</h2>
        <p>Must be programmed if <a href="ext-trcrsctlrn.html">TRCRSCTLR&lt;a&gt;</a>.GROUP == <span class="binarynumber">0b0010</span> and <a href="ext-trcrsctlrn.html">TRCRSCTLR&lt;a&gt;</a>.COUNTERS[n] == 1.</p>

      
        <p>If the trace unit is not in the Idle state it is <span class="arm-defined-word">CONSTRAINED UNPREDICTABLE</span> whether writes to this register are ignored.</p>

      
        <p>Reads from this register might return an <span class="arm-defined-word">UNKNOWN</span> value if the trace unit is not in either of the Idle or Stable states.</p>
      <h4>TRCCNTVR&lt;n&gt; can be accessed through the external debug interface:</h4><table class="info"><tr><th>Component</th><th>Offset</th><th>Instance</th></tr><tr><td>ETE</td><td><span class="hexnumber">0x160</span> + (4 * n)</td><td>TRCCNTVR&lt;n&gt;</td></tr></table><p>Accessible as follows:</p><ul><li>When OSLockStatus(), or !AllowExternalTraceAccess(addrdesc), or !IsTraceCorePowered(), accesses to this register generate an error response.
          </li><li>When n &gt;= NUM_TRACE_COUNTERS, accesses to this register are <span class="access_level">RES0</span>.
          </li><li>Otherwise, accesses to this register are <span class="access_level">RW</span>.
          </li></ul><hr class="bottom_line"></hr><p class="copyconf">Version 2026.09 — Copyright © 2010-2026 Arm Limited or its affiliates.</p><small>This site is provided as a community resource and is NOT affiliated with nor endorsed by Arm Limited.</small><!-- Cloudflare Pages Analytics --><script defer src='https://static.cloudflareinsights.com/beacon.min.js' data-cf-beacon='{"token": "de55e78a4e194365a81a0724c5c0ee91"}'></script><!-- Cloudflare Pages Analytics --></body></html>
